
# HSH2026 RESEARCH COMMONS LICENSE AND COMMERCIAL ACCESS TERMS

**Version 1.0 — Effective September 4, 2026**

**Archive:** HSH2026 — H(s)H / Hyper(super)helical Worldtube Research Archive  
**Canonical archive:** https://github.com/Satobloc/HsH  
**Originator:** Nathan McKnight / Nathan J. Bellomy  
**ORCID:** https://orcid.org/0009-0006-2462-0062
**Contact:** scalarangulartheory@gmail.com

## 1. Purpose

HSH2026 is maintained as an open research, development, and provenance archive.

Its purpose is to permit broad access to an evolving body of theoretical, geometric, mathematical, computational, methodological, philosophical, and explanatory work while preserving:

- open scientific and academic inquiry;
- reasonable attribution and historical provenance;
- meaningful participation by the originator when protected archive material becomes a substantial source of private commercial value; and
- at exceptional scale, some meaningful return of resulting value to the wider commons.

The archive holder does not object to commerce, profit, employment, private enterprise, or the creation of useful technologies merely because they involve ideas encountered through this archive.

The concern is narrower:

**Material private economic value should not be systematically extracted from protected HSH2026 material while its identifiable source contribution is erased and its originator excluded from the resulting value.**

Nothing in these terms claims ownership of facts, mathematical truths, laws of nature, independently discovered ideas, physical reality, or other subject matter that applicable law does not permit the archive holder to control.

## 2. Covered Material

These terms apply, to the extent Nathan McKnight / Nathan J. Bellomy owns or controls rights capable of being licensed, to original copyrightable research and archive material associated with H(s)H and its development.

Covered Material may include qualifying:

- notes and manuscripts;
- conversations and human-authored conversational contributions;
- diagrams and explanatory materials;
- geometric and representational systems;
- research summaries;
- mathematical and formalization attempts;
- methodological materials;
- simulations and computational materials;
- prediction and test records;
- compilations and arrangements;
- AI-assisted research materials;
- and other original project materials.

H(s)H, Hyperhelical Worldtube, Hyper(super)helical Worldtube, and related terminology used within this archive should be understood as parts of an evolving research programme unless otherwise stated.

## 3. Default Public License

Except where otherwise marked, Covered Material is made available for noncommercial use under:

**Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International — CC BY-NC 4.0**

https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/

The additional academic, research, and commercial permissions contained below are separate grants from the archive holder and do not modify the standard Creative Commons license.

## 4. Independent Research and Academic Open Access

Independent researchers, individual academics, students, teachers, academic research programmes, scholarly collaborations, and bona fide academic or scientific users may research, study, test, criticize, teach, formalize, simulate, reproduce, quote, adapt, and build research programmes around Covered Material without fee or separate permission, subject to reasonable attribution.

This remains free and open regardless of ordinary institutional affiliation or research funding, provided the use is genuinely academic, scholarly, educational, or investigative in character and is not principally being conducted as part of a plan to create, develop, or operate a commercial business based upon Covered Material or resulting developments.

In plain language:

**Research it for free. Study it for free. Teach it for free. Build an academic research programme around it for free. If the plan becomes making a business out of it, the commercial terms begin to apply.**

## 5. Attribution and Provenance

Reasonable attribution is required where Covered Material is reproduced, adapted, incorporated, or materially relied upon in circumstances where attribution would ordinarily be meaningful.

No single citation style is mandatory. Equivalent scholarly, technical, bibliographic, legal, or house styles are acceptable.

### HSH2026 citation

**Nathan McKnight / Nathan J. Bellomy, ORCID [INSERT ORCID], HSH2026 — H(s)H / Hyper(super)helical Worldtube Research Archive, https://github.com/Satobloc/HsH, accessed [DATE].**

Compact form:

**HSH2026, https://github.com/Satobloc/HsH, accessed [DATE].**

Targeted form:

**Nathan McKnight, ORCID [INSERT ORCID], HSH2026, “[FILE / SECTION / SUBADDRESS],” https://github.com/Satobloc/HsH, accessed [DATE].**

### SB2325 citation

The principal predecessor and developmental archive is:

**Nathan McKnight / Nathan J. Bellomy, ORCID [INSERT ORCID], SB2325 Theoretical Sandbox — RMS / SAT Research Archive, https://github.com/Satobloc/SAT_THEORY_ARCHIVE_2023-25, accessed [DATE].**

Compact form:

**SB2325 Theoretical Sandbox, https://github.com/Satobloc/SAT_THEORY_ARCHIVE_2023-25, accessed [DATE].**

Where a work materially draws upon both developmental periods, citation of both archives is encouraged.

Attribution to either **Nathan McKnight** or **Nathan J. Bellomy** is acceptable. Where practical, linking both names is preferred to preserve continuity across publication and citation records.

Attribution does not imply endorsement. A researcher may cite either archive while rejecting H(s)H, SAT, RMS, or any surrounding theoretical interpretation.

## 6. Relationship to SB2325

HSH2026 continues a research lineage whose earlier development is documented principally in the SB2325 Theoretical Sandbox:

https://github.com/Satobloc/SAT_THEORY_ARCHIVE_2023-25

Users of both archives are **requested, but not legally required by this HSH2026 license, to treat SB2325 material in accordance with the same general research, attribution, commercial-access, and reciprocity principles expressed here wherever they are voluntarily able to do so.**

This is a request for continuity of practice and provenance.

It is **not** a condition imposed by HSH2026 upon access to SB2325, and nothing in this document alters whatever legal permissions independently govern material in SB2325.

## 7. Commercial Research Early Supporter Open Access Pass

A commercial researcher, company, laboratory, research organization, or other commercial entity may obtain a **Commercial Research Early Supporter Open Access Pass** for a one-time payment of:

**US $5,000**

The pass grants continuing commercial research access to Covered Material, subject to reasonable attribution and one principal reciprocal condition:

**Substantive research findings arising from use of HSH2026 must be made openly available to the public within a reasonable period.**

Legitimate temporary limitations may apply where necessary for safety, security, privacy, regulation, peer review, or protection of genuinely independent inventions.

The Early Supporter Pass authorizes research, analysis, testing, prototyping, formalization, simulation, and development.

It does not:

- transfer ownership of HSH2026;
- grant rights in third-party material;
- grant patent rights unless expressly stated;
- authorize false claims of authorship or provenance;
- permit sublicensing the archive itself as a competing commercial corpus;
- or automatically settle terms for substantial downstream commercialization.

Once granted, an Early Supporter Pass will not be repriced merely because HSH2026 later becomes unexpectedly valuable.

To obtain the pass, contact Nathan McKnight / Nathan J. Bellomy at scalarangulartheory@gmail.com for payment instructions and written acknowledgment of the grant.

## 8. Systematic Commercial Archive Mining

A substantial commercial organization wishing to systematically search, computationally mine, ingest, analyze, or otherwise use HSH2026 as a continuing source of research directions, technical structures, representations, formalizations, methods, or potentially exploitable developments may obtain a:

**Commercial Archive Mining / Open Research Access License — US $10,000 per annum**

This annual license authorizes commercial research and systematic archive mining during the paid period, subject to reasonable attribution and provenance.

It does **not** constitute a purchase of the archive or a buyout of rights relating to commercially significant technologies subsequently derived from protected HSH2026 material.

In plain language:

**US $10,000 per year buys permission to mine HSH2026 as a commercial R&D resource. It does not buy HSH2026 or automatically buy every major downstream commercial right.**

## 9. Ordinary Commercial Development

Commercial activity is not categorically prohibited.

Small-scale, exploratory, incidental, experimental, or otherwise non-substantial commercial development may proceed under the standing permissions of this license where the resulting activity has not become Material HSH-Dependent Commercial Use.

The purpose of this provision is to avoid creating unnecessary barriers for individual developers, small enterprises, early prototypes, experimental applications, or other ordinary attempts to discover whether anything useful can be made from the research.

Reasonable attribution remains required.

## 10. Material HSH-Dependent Commercial Use

Commercial activity becomes **Material HSH-Dependent Commercial Use** when both of the following become substantially true:

### A. Material dependence

HSH2026 or identifiable Covered Material materially contributes to the commercial development through one or more of:

- specific protected technical material;
- a distinctive project-specific representation or explanatory structure;
- methodologies or formalization strategies;
- research directions;
- computational or mathematical developments;
- repeated use of archive material;
- derived implementations;
- or systematic use of multiple identifiable lines of development from the archive.

### B. Material commercial significance

The resulting activity has become commercially substantial enough that continued use of the protected contribution is no longer reasonably characterized as exploratory, incidental, or minor.

No single correspondence is required where the overall commercial programme exhibits substantial and repeated dependence upon HSH2026.

## 11. Systematic Extraction and Aggregate Dependence

Repeated or systematic use of HSH2026 as a source of commercially exploitable concepts, methods, formalizations, representations, research directions, implementations, or derivative technical developments may constitute Material HSH-Dependent Commercial Use even where no single extracted item would independently satisfy that standard.

An organization whose research process substantially consists of searching HSH2026 for promising structures and repeatedly converting them into proprietary products, patents, processes, or commercial research advantages may therefore fall within this provision because of the **aggregate relationship**.

This provision distinguishes ordinary intellectual influence from systematic commercial mining of the research corpus.

## 12. Meaningful Commercial Participation

Material HSH-Dependent Commercial Use requires a separate commercial agreement with Nathan McKnight / Nathan J. Bellomy.

Such an agreement should provide **meaningful personal economic participation reasonably proportionate to the identifiable contribution and resulting commercial value.**

Possible arrangements include:

- royalties;
- profit participation;
- equity;
- lump-sum compensation;
- recurring payments;
- funded research or development support;
- salary, fellowship, consultancy, or comparable support where mutually desired;
- or another mutually agreed arrangement.

The intended standard is not merely nominal acknowledgment.

Where protected HSH2026 material has become a material foundation for substantial private value creation, compensation should represent a **real and livable participation in that value** rather than symbolic remuneration.

Specific terms are negotiated according to the circumstances of the use.

## 13. Attribution Does Not Substitute for Compensation

For Material HSH-Dependent Commercial Use, citation alone does not satisfy the commercial-license requirement.

Likewise, payment does not eliminate ordinary provenance obligations.

At substantial commercial scale, the intended relationship is:

**acknowledgment + meaningful participation.**

## 14. Exceptional-Scale Use and Commons Reciprocity

Where HSH-dependent commercial use becomes exceptionally consequential in economic, technological, or infrastructural scale, meaningful personal participation by the originator remains applicable and an additional meaningful benefit should flow to the wider commons.

Commons Reciprocity may be satisfied through one or more mutually reasonable mechanisms, including:

- open publication of consequential research or technical knowledge;
- royalty-free public, scientific, educational, or humanitarian access;
- broad public availability of resulting capabilities;
- open standards or specifications;
- public-interest licensing;
- contributions supporting housing, food, healthcare, basic security, infrastructure, education, research access, or related public goods;
- contribution to an appropriate public-benefit or commons mechanism;
- or another arrangement having substantially comparable public effect.

The exact mechanism need not be identical for every technology or industry.

Safety, security, privacy, environmental impact, regulatory obligations, or other genuine practical constraints may justify alternatives to unrestricted publication.

The requirement is intended to produce a **meaningful return flow**, not mechanically identical disclosure.

## 15. Personal Participation and Commons Reciprocity Are Distinct

A public-benefit contribution does not automatically substitute for fair participation by the archive originator.

Likewise, compensation to the archive originator does not necessarily satisfy an exceptional-scale Commons Reciprocity obligation.

At sufficiently consequential scale, the intended structure is:

**The originator participates meaningfully in the value created, while some portion of extraordinary value also returns to the broader commons.**

## 16. Independent Development

These terms do not claim control over genuinely independent work merely because it resembles H(s)H or reaches comparable mathematical, geometric, or physical conclusions.

Similarity alone is not sufficient.

Priority, provenance, copyright, patentability, and licensing are separate questions.

Nothing here converts independently discovered facts, mathematical relationships, physical principles, or independently created implementations into Covered Material merely because similar material appears in HSH2026.

## 17. Patents and Specific Inventions

No patent license is granted by this document unless expressly stated.

These terms also do not claim patent rights that do not exist.

Public disclosure of a scientific idea, mathematical relationship, representational system, or technical possibility should not be interpreted as an assertion that the archive holder owns every later implementation.

Specific patentable inventions, if any, may be separately identified and licensed.

## 18. AI-Assisted and AI-Generated Material

HSH2026 may contain extensive interaction with computational systems and large language models.

Nathan McKnight / Nathan J. Bellomy does not represent that every word, equation, paragraph, diagram, or formalization contained in the archive was personally authored by him.

The archive records a directed research process in which human contributions may include originating concepts, supplying geometric structures, establishing constraints, explaining intended meaning, directing formalization, correcting outputs, selecting or rejecting proposals, designing methodologies, arranging materials, and preserving developmental provenance.

AI-generated material is licensed only to the extent that the archive holder possesses rights capable of being licensed.

Nothing here asserts copyright in material that applicable law regards as uncopyrightable.

## 19. Third-Party Material

Third-party papers, publications, photographs, datasets, quotations, software, images, recordings, and other externally authored material are excluded from this license except where the archive holder separately possesses authority to license them.

Their inclusion for archival, research, critical, or historical purposes does not constitute a claim of ownership.

## 20. Software and Archive Tools

Software, scripts, indexing systems, archive tools, extraction utilities, and similar executable or source-code material may carry separate software licenses.

Where a software file or directory contains a specific license notice, that license governs that software.

## 21. Music, Artwork, Recordings, and Other Creative Works

Standalone music, sound recordings, artwork, photography, fiction, album materials, and other creative works appearing in or alongside the repository are excluded from these research terms unless expressly designated otherwise.

Their applicable rights are reserved or separately licensed.

## 22. Voluntary Legacy and Cross-Archive Reciprocity

Anyone who has already derived substantial commercial value from work documented in SB2325 is invited to acknowledge that value voluntarily through attribution, support, commercial regularization, or adoption of the HSH2026 reciprocity principles.

No obligation under this section is asserted merely by virtue of past access to SB2325.

Organizations or individuals who voluntarily regularize an existing relationship with the earlier archive may contact the archive holder to discuss favorable continuing access to HSH2026.

## 23. Good-Faith Interpretation

These terms are intended to facilitate research, scholarship, experimentation, and ordinary productive use rather than manufacture accidental violations.

Minor citation defects, ambiguous edge cases, good-faith scholarly use, and reasonable disagreement about provenance should ordinarily be resolved through correction and discussion rather than punitive enforcement.

The more demanding commercial provisions are directed primarily at:

**substantial, systematic, economically consequential exploitation of protected archive material.**

## 24. No Warranty

Covered Material is provided for research and exploratory use without warranty of correctness, completeness, fitness for a particular purpose, noninfringement, safety, or physical validity.

Use of the material is at the user's own risk.

